hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"76","It is narrated from Umm al-Mu'mineen Sayyida Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) that when the Noble Prophet ﷺ would conclude the prayer with salam, the women would get up immediately after the salam, and the Noble Prophet ﷺ would remain seated in his place for a short while. Ibn Shihab al-Zuhri (may Allah have mercy on him) says that in our opinion, the Prophet ﷺ would remain seated for a short while so that the women could leave before the men stood up."
